This program implements a Standard Variational Autoencoder (S-VAE) for high-dimensional trajectory data from linear time-invariant (LTI) systems. 
Designed to handle large-scale state-control trajectories, the model features a encoder-decoder architecture with Layer Normalization to stabilize training across five hidden layers.
The training objective combines mean squared reconstruction loss with KL divergence to learn compressed, generative latent representations. 
After training, the decoder is used to synthesize 1000 realistic trajectory samples, aiding in simulation, data augmentation, or downstream control tasks.
